From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:57:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] camera: device@1.0: support MediaTek legacy HAL1 modules

Two assumptions of MediaTek's HAL1 camera modules (libcam.client) that
held before O:

- The buffer_handle_t* returned by dequeue_buffer points at the handle
  member of an ANativeWindowBuffer; the module steps back to the
  enclosing buffer and calls common.incRef/decRef on it. Keep each
  preview buffer handle inside a real ANativeWindowBuffer with the
  preview geometry and no-op refcount hooks.
- The request_memory and data callbacks may be called with a NULL user
  cookie. Fall back to the currently open device.
---
